[[0,1328607,0,1,2,-1,"2016-10-06T01:02:04","answermarket","",[],"<p><a href=\"http://answer.market/\">http://answer.market/</a></p>\n<p>Did you know that free.market costs $55k? Pretty crazy.</p>\n<p>It's ugly. It takes only Bitcoin. Let me know what you goats think.</p>","I launched a website to make me money","","whatever"],[1,6494319,0,2,0,2,"2016-10-06T01:43:35","Diogenes_The_Cynic","",[],"<p>This is cool, but whats to stop people from getting a second rate answer instead of a first? There seems to be no filter.</p>"],[2,6494502,6494319,1,0,1,"2016-10-06T02:13:50","answermarket","",[],"<p>There isn't any filter. They will have to vet it themselves based on the quality of the sample, and the reputation of the identity that's posting the answer.</p>\n<p>So if Linus Torvalds posts one of those for a Linux question, it's probably worth buying. If a 0-day old Voat account posts a $10 answer with a crappy sample, I wouldn't buy it.</p>"],[3,6495251,6494502,1,0,1,"2016-10-06T04:36:53","Diogenes_The_Cynic","",[],"<p>This needs some kind of how-to for people to know what they're buying and how it works. Unless they're familiar with it, and already existing customers, the barrier to entry (what is this) will be too high.</p>"]]
